{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies","id":1178534,"title":"Cancer Conspiracies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-23T13:33:28-08:00","id":1178534,"title":"Cancer Conspiracies","content":"This topic is about listing and brain-storming Hunter Conspiracies that are backed by the monsters themselves. To fit this definition of a Cancer Conspiracy, they:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Must be a full Conspiracy (and thus, have an Endowment - exception being made if the Compact is being run with an Endowment)</li> <li>The Endowment must be sourced from a known monster (the reader needs to know and identify the monster, even if the members don't know)</li> <li>The Conspiracy must be controlled or excessively influenced by the monster in question</li> <li>They still hunt other monsters and generally still uphold the Vigil</li> </ol>The key point is - if the monster(s) were removed, the Conspiracy would collapse or be fundamentally change. <br /> <hr /><br /> On to examples.<br /> <br /> The Knights of St. Adrian and the Les Mysteres are clear examples, backed by an Angel and Spirits (respectively). The Malleus Malficarum's and Cainite Heresy's backers are too vague to count, The Cheiron Group's Board is optional (and their Endowment source is too diverse), Task Force: VALKYRIE <i>may</i> be influenced by Vampires, but their power isn't derived from them.<br /> <br /> New examples might easily be:<ul><li>Vampire: A Conspiracy of actual Ghouls (or just Vitae users).</li> <li>Werewolf: A confederation (or even Lodge) of Wolf-Blooded and normal humans.</li> <li>Demon: A cabal of hackers that use a server of Software Gadgets.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T15:16:22-08:00","id":1178567,"title":"","content":"Got an idea that I never fleshed out that meets the requirements.<br /> <br /> - Geist: a 19th century born occult society of mediums. The founders had a shared out-of-body experience and travelled in the Underworld. Things went bad and some nasty ghost/Cthonian/abomination from beyond the world of the living destroyed them and took possess of their body. They're still around, pretending to be the human founders empowered by their experience. They anoint the Hunters with ectoplasm and grant them powers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T16:14:48-08:00","id":1178585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178567#post1178567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got an idea that I never fleshed out that meets the requirements.<br /> <br /> - Geist: a 19th century born occult society of mediums. The founders had a shared out-of-body experience and travelled in the Underworld. Things went bad and some nasty ghost/Cthonian/abomination from beyond the world of the living destroyed them and took possess of their body. They're still around, pretending to be the human founders empowered by their experience. They anoint the Hunters with ectoplasm and grant them powers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. What kind of powers? Ghostly ones, obviously, but are you thinking Numina, Influences, or new powers for the Endowment? (Did Ceremonies require Plasm?)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, Geist had Fetters - Ghosts bound into their last Anchor. Sin-Eaters could use one of the Ghost's Numina for 1 Willpower. What if they are given the ability to use them and make them as well (kind of like a more specialized Relic). If the being is a Cthonian, it might even hunger for Ghosts too, which gives a motivation for bringing back the spectres they &quot;bust&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-23-2018, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:22:42-08:00","id":1178605,"title":"","content":"The Goetic Gospels of the Knights of Saint George may be powered by Anunnaki, from what I\u2019ve heard in the forums. (Don\u2019t have Hunter 1E supplements, so not sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:38:13-08:00","id":1178614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178605#post1178605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Goetic Gospels of the Knights of Saint George may be powered by Anunnaki, from what I\u2019ve heard in the forums. (Don\u2019t have Hunter 1E supplements, so not sure)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>May</i> is the important word here, I think. They very well could be - but we don't <i>know</i>, like we do with the Les Mysteres and St. Adrian. Definitely a fringe/maybe case, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:12:29-08:00","id":1178633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178585#post1178585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. What kind of powers? Ghostly ones, obviously, but are you thinking Numina, Influences, or new powers for the Endowment? (Did Ceremonies require Plasm?)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, Geist had Fetters - Ghosts bound into their last Anchor. Sin-Eaters could use one of the Ghost's Numina for 1 Willpower. What if they are given the ability to use them and make them as well (kind of like a more specialized Relic). If the being is a Cthonian, it might even hunger for Ghosts too, which gives a motivation for bringing back the spectres they &quot;bust&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never got around to actually give serious thought about their Endowment. They are inspired by those old weird &quot;medium channeling ectoplasm&quot; pictures, so the pictures I had of it was spooky/medium powers. Using Fetters and Numina might be smarter than whatever I had in mind (which was a bunch of half-baked, bizzarre ideas)<br /> <br /> The Cthonian eating ghosts was actually the excuse I came up with for the Hunters to remain active, so I'm with you in that one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:20:52-08:00","id":1178637,"title":"","content":"Theres that theory that the AKD are an unknowing Mummy cult. Does that count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:42:59-08:00","id":1178642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178633#post1178633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never got around to actually give serious thought about their Endowment. They are inspired by those old weird &quot;medium channeling ectoplasm&quot; pictures, so the pictures I had of it was spooky/medium powers. Using Fetters and Numina might be smarter than whatever I had in mind (which was a bunch of half-baked, bizzarre ideas)<br /> <br /> The Cthonian eating ghosts was actually the excuse I came up with for the Hunters to remain active, so I'm with you in that one</div> </div> </div> </div>Another idea was using Death Masks (from deceased Geists) and tapping into that crazy 1E Manifestation goodness, but that might be more work and justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178637#post1178637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres that theory that the AKD are an unknowing Mummy cult. Does that count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theories. It isn't established as fact (even if they character in universe don't realize it). Strix could be the Messengers for the Cainite Heresy, and the God-Machine could be powering Benedictions, but we don't <i>know</i>, or it is left to Storytellers. This is for those where we do, in fact, know the source responsible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:09:41-08:00","id":1178664,"title":"","content":"In my sig you could find Tartarus Enterprise, which are a Cancer Conspiracy by definition- not only that they work with monsters, they actually fight hunters in order to protect them and achieve their vision of a world powered by the miracles of technology and monstrous power. So what if a vampire needs to drink a mortal to death once and awhile, or a demon has to steal the soul of a mortal to exist? Its only a small price to pay in exchange for the wonders they can achieve together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T01:29:31-08:00","id":1178703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178614#post1178614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>May</i> is the important word here, I think. They very well could be - but we don't <i>know</i>, like we do with the Les Mysteres and St. Adrian. Definitely a fringe/maybe case, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the God-machine is ever explicitly mentioned. The Knights work for an 'angel' with weird tech themed magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:41:45-08:00","id":1178738,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea after five minutes of thought and a cup of coffee:<br /> <br /> Beast: A Tyrant Incarnate has decided that it wants to be the Apex of the entire world. It brings mortals under its power through its Myth of being the secret, darkling Lord of the Earth's Shadows. Its hunters go out and browbeat other monsters into pledging fealty to it, oftentimes working to destabilize or subvert supernatural hierarchies. I guess their Endowment could be an extension of Kinship abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:54:33-08:00","id":1178745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178738#post1178738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea after five minutes of thought and a cup of coffee:<br /> <br /> Beast: A Tyrant Incarnate has decided that it wants to be the Apex of the entire world. It brings mortals under its power through its Myth of being the secret, darkling Lord of the Earth's Shadows. Its hunters go out and browbeat other monsters into pledging fealty to it, oftentimes working to destabilize or subvert supernatural hierarchies. I guess their Endowment could be an extension of Kinship abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please clarify on the Kinship abilities. Like &quot;Hey, we are family&quot; social effects? &quot;I can drink blood too&quot;? Use of Kinship Nightmares?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:01:52-08:00","id":1178748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178745#post1178745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please clarify on the Kinship abilities. Like &quot;Hey, we are family&quot; social effects? &quot;I can drink blood too&quot;? Use of Kinship Nightmares?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I imagine something like the ability to get a sense when monsters are around, maybe being able to impose the Family Ties Condition (though it's connected to the Incarnate, not the hunter), perhaps even at higher levels being able to develop abilities that are similar to Kinship Nightmares from convincing enough monsters of a certain type to swear fealty to Tyrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:03:02-08:00","id":1178984,"title":"","content":"If the answer to &quot;Which conspiracies are cancerous?&quot; isn't &quot;all of them&quot;, something went wrong. THe various states of compromise for power is entirely the point.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the answer really is &quot;All of them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:43:23-08:00","id":1178997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178984#post1178984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the answer to &quot;Which conspiracies are cancerous?&quot; isn't &quot;all of them&quot;, something went wrong. THe various states of compromise for power is entirely the point.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the answer really is &quot;All of them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I defined it above. In a non-philosophical/rhetorical sense. So it wouldn't encompass all the groups. Hunter has a fairly specific definition for &quot;Cancer&quot; in the context of a Cell, and I'm just expanding it to cover Conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T17:30:43-08:00","id":1179022,"title":"","content":"The Starlight Guardians are secretly backed by True Fae Exiles trying to spitefully throw wrenches into the plans of other True Fae and Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:53:33-08:00","id":1179319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1178984#post1178984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the answer to &quot;Which conspiracies are cancerous?&quot; isn't &quot;all of them&quot;, something went wrong. THe various states of compromise for power is entirely the point.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the answer really is &quot;All of them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, conspiracies don't *have* to be cancerous. TFV is one example, fancy guns don't make you less human. While the vampires might be pulling the strings and funding all the research that gives the group its &quot;powers&quot;, it could theoretically work without them. The &quot;Other Countries also have TFV equivalents&quot; thing means that there is possibly a group of government-sponsored hunters that arn't also vampire sponsored.<br /> <br /> It just involves getting not-so-supernatural powers from a human source, while keeping from becoming a puppet of everything that wants to use use for its own gain. Easier said then done, but not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:05:26-08:00","id":1179330,"title":"","content":"I think the point was more that if you have an international conspiracy you're missing out on something if they are all, somehow, a unified front without any external influence from the various powers that love influencing such things.<br /> <br /> And Task Force Valkyrie's problem isn't just the vampires, its the whole taking down other hunters thing, as well, like in Project EINHERJAR.<br /> <br /> Given the widespread nature of government corruption, the 'other countries with TFV equivalents' would likely see similar problems. If they're not vampires, they could be other issues.<br /> <br /> A argument could be made about 'cancer' conspiracies and whether they are actually as negative as they're made out to be, but the thread is more about listing the ones, fanmade or in canon.<br /> <br /> My pitch for Qing Dynasty China had hunters working for the Pure-run Empire to bring down outlaws and dissidents who were, mainly, Forsaken and spirits that refused to work with the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2018, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:59:10-08:00","id":1179352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179330#post1179330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point was more that if you have an international conspiracy you're missing out on something if they are all, somehow, a unified front without any external influence from the various powers that love influencing such things.<br /> <br /> And Task Force Valkyrie's problem isn't just the vampires, its the whole taking down other hunters thing, as well, like in Project EINHERJAR.<br /> <br /> Given the widespread nature of government corruption, the 'other countries with TFV equivalents' would likely see similar problems. If they're not vampires, they could be other issues.<br /> <br /> A argument could be made about 'cancer' conspiracies and whether they are actually as negative as they're made out to be, but the thread is more about listing the ones, fanmade or in canon.<br /> <br /> My pitch for Qing Dynasty China had hunters working for the Pure-run Empire to bring down outlaws and dissidents who were, mainly, Forsaken and spirits that refused to work with the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are confusing your definitions. &quot;Cancer&quot; cells are cells with supernatural members. &quot;Cancer Conspiracies&quot; are basically the conspiracy version of a Cancer Cell, as described in the OP. This isn't necessarily a bad thing-a group with supernatural members or backing can be better or worse than those without it. Its a bad thing in the eyes of many Hunters, thus the negative description. TFV may have more problems than just vampires running it, but having vampires running it is the &quot;Cancer&quot; part. A theoretical Chinese TFV that kills Hunters and dissidents while using similarly advanced technology isn't a cancer conspiracy, unless another group of vampires is calling the shots. Even if it is still marred in bureaucracy, corruption, and other problems with government jobs, it isn't a &quot;Cancer Conspiracy&quot;. Having Vampires and what have you occasionally doing the corruption or occasionally joining in at the cell level isn't enough to turn it into a Cancer conspiracy, in the same way a cell getting anonymous tips from a Vampire doesn't turn them into a cancer cell.<br /> <br /> In the end, you can be influenced by something without being controlled by it. Cancer Conspiracies are controlled by it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:04:05-08:00","id":1179357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179352#post1179352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, you can be influenced by something without being controlled by it. Cancer Conspiracies are controlled by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, for the purposes of this classification/discussion, empowered by it. I'm not counting TF:V because you could cut the Vampire influence and it would change little. The same cannot be said about the Les Mysteres. Cut the Spirits out and they... don't really exist anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:06:34-08:00","id":1179358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179352#post1179352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A theoretical Chinese TFV that kills Hunters and dissidents while using similarly advanced technology isn't a cancer conspiracy, unless another group of vampires is calling the shots. Even if it is still marred in bureaucracy, corruption, and other problems with government jobs, it isn't a &quot;Cancer Conspiracy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The theoretical conspiracy was actively working for a faction of antagonist werewolves, they're called the Pure. They would have been further empowered by the general rites and abilities granted by lodges and packs, as well as knowledge of how to block spirits and defeat werewolves, ideally the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">n the end, you can be influenced by something without being controlled by it. Cancer Conspiracies are controlled by it.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Are you sure you're not confusing definitions? Just going by Vent0's opening post you can see it can be influenced ('excessively) or controlled.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies#post1178534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Conspiracy must be controlled or excessively influenced by the monster in question</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2018, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:30:36-08:00","id":1179369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179357#post1179357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, for the purposes of this classification/discussion, empowered by it. I'm not counting TF:V because you could cut the Vampire influence and it would change little. The same cannot be said about the Les Mysteres. Cut the Spirits out and they... don't really exist anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I did read your OP. Which is why ArcaneArt's comment was confusing.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, would the Lucifuge count? The system usually treats them as humans, but they are controlled by an ambiguous monstrous leader and are empowered by demons. Judging by your example, it would not be considered due to the ambiguous situation (and probably the fact that the Lucifuge probably isn't the one dolling out powers personally).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theoretical conspiracy was actively working for a faction of antagonist werewolves, they're called the Pure. They would have been further empowered by the general rites and abilities granted by lodges and packs, as well as knowledge of how to block spirits and defeat werewolves, ideally the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about a different theoretical conspiracy that wasn't influenced by any supernatural, as an example. Though I could see how that would get confusing. Probably should have said &quot;Russia&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Are you sure you're not confusing definitions? Just going by Vent0's opening post you can see it can be influenced ('excessively) or controlled.</span> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure. Influenced excessively is the same as controlling it. As long as the influence is non &quot;excessive&quot;, it isn't controlled.<br /> <br /> A Vampire bribing Russian TFV brass to take out a rival is influencing it. It is not 'excessive'-the conspiracy doesn't become the vampire's personal hit-men due to this influence being present. They may be defined by corruption, but a normal mob boss could theoretically do the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:38:06-08:00","id":1179372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179369#post1179369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic, would the Lucifuge count? The system usually treats them as humans, but they are controlled by an ambiguous monstrous leader and are empowered by demons. Judging by your example, it would not be considered due to the ambiguous situation (and probably the fact that the Lucifuge probably isn't the one dolling out powers personally).</div> </div> </div> </div>Full conspiracy, Endowment is sourced by a known monster (demons). Controlled or excessively influenced by the monster in question. Still hunt monsters and uphold the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Vent0 seems to not allow for ambiguity so I'd say no. The Lucifuge is controlling them, but no one knows what her agenda is and whether she's for or against the demons the powers come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T08:52:10-08:00","id":1179524,"title":"","content":"An obvious choice for a cancer conspiracy would be one including mages who use their magic to empower or equip mortal hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:28:09-08:00","id":1179573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179524#post1179524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An obvious choice for a cancer conspiracy would be one including mages who use their magic to empower or equip mortal hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a Division Six with actual support?<br /> <br /> They would either have to have indirect support (scrying, &quot;coincidental&quot; fortune, etc.) - which wouldn't really count, I'd think - or members would have to be Sleepwalkers. Or, I suppose, <i>made</i> Sleepwalkers with Stealing Fire. That's definitely one way to ensure employee retention: You can resign at any time, but your mind might break from all the things you saw on the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:09:07-08:00","id":1179586,"title":"","content":"So thinking about it, while Tartarus are outright Cancer Conspiracy, some of my other conspiracies may also fall under that definition, according to the way that Vent0 has presented it. Raziel Ltd, for example, is backed by an (the!) Exile Angel. The Silver Syndicate have the help of a local Spirit Noble. The Followers of Set work with and for vampires. The Mori Kage fulfill contracts signed with the True Fae. The Heirs of the Crone exist out of a pact with a demon lord. Others may also be considered as Cancer Organizations, depending on where exactly you draw the line (the Silent Imperative, for example, work against hunters to save &quot;innocent monsters&quot;. The Pythian Oracles are being led by a Body Thief which use a the minds of others in order to compute her &quot;perfect future&quot;, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:05:51-08:00","id":1179831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1179573#post1179573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would either have to have indirect support (scrying, &quot;coincidental&quot; fortune, etc.) - which wouldn't really count, I'd think - or members would have to be Sleepwalkers. Or, I suppose, <i>made</i> Sleepwalkers with Stealing Fire. That's definitely one way to ensure employee retention: You can resign at any time, but your mind might break from all the things you saw on the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that, or they would have to be convinced somehow that the mages are mages, but also of this limitation about magic being used directly alongside them - it would be one way to make the mages and hunters deploy separately.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T04:15:55-08:00","id":1180660,"title":"","content":"For me one of the more interesting things about Hunter is that none of them are that effective at what they do because the other game lines still exist. But when you look at it all compacts and conspiracies out there exist in one of the below four categories:<br /> <br /> - Well-meaning and possibly even effective at a local level, but they don't really treat the symptoms or are effective in the grand scheme of things.<br /> - They either have no idea what they're doing or make the jobs of other people/monsters more difficult.<br /> - Cults in service to a monster or unwitting tools of one.<br /> - Monsters (or something close to them) in their own right or actively making things worse for everyone.<br /> <br /> But that's the charm of Hunter: The Vigil. It's not about saving the world, but trying to make it better for yourself and the people around you. And eventually you will be snuffed out in one of many ways, but this will light two more flames. Your vigil will end, but the Vigil will continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T17:45:44-08:00","id":1180943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1180660#post1180660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me one of the more interesting things about Hunter is that none of them are that effective at what they do because the other game lines still exist. But when you look at it all compacts and conspiracies out there exist in one of the below four categories:<br /> <br /> - Well-meaning and possibly even effective at a local level, but they don't really treat the symptoms or are effective in the grand scheme of things.<br /> - They either have no idea what they're doing or make the jobs of other people/monsters more difficult.<br /> - Cults in service to a monster or unwitting tools of one.<br /> - Monsters (or something close to them) in their own right or actively making things worse for everyone.<br /> <br /> But that's the charm of Hunter: The Vigil. It's not about saving the world, but trying to make it better for yourself and the people around you. And eventually you will be snuffed out in one of many ways, but this will light two more flames. Your vigil will end, but the Vigil will continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say the same things about the other gamelines too, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:04:52-08:00","id":1181047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1180943#post1180943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say the same things about the other gamelines too, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since those don't have the theme of the Vigil, I'd say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:06:56-08:00","id":1181642,"title":"","content":"While it would be a cancer compact rather than conspiracy, a group like the Union who outright allied with the local werewolf pack (in Werewolf the Forsaken terms, they would presumably be human members of the pack) is something I would expect to have happened from time to time.<br /> <br /> Glamourweaver's KSI-21 is a Soviet-descended conspiracy that uses weird tech to allow its hunters to astrally project and gain other quasi-ghostly powers. Geist the Sin-Eaters refers to a Sin-Eater conspiracy in much the same place and time, and I suggested that the former was an attempt to replicate the abilities of the latter.* But if that's so, there's no reason to rule out the Sin-Eaters actually cooperating with such an endeavour (maybe even kicking it off) - in which case, KSI-21 might still have Sin-Eaters in it working alongside the projecting humans.<br /> <br /> * In hindsight, bet they made some Deviants along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:31:59-08:00","id":1181708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1181642#post1181642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it would be a cancer compact rather than conspiracy, a group like the Union who outright allied with the local werewolf pack (in Werewolf the Forsaken terms, they would presumably be human members of the pack) is something I would expect to have happened from time to time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more of a Cancer <i>Cell</i>, and regardless, outside the bounds I listed. <br /> <br /> Because seriously - if any Hunter group that had some involvement with monsters applied, there would be no distinction because they would all be guilty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1181642#post1181642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glamourweaver's KSI-21 is a Soviet-descended conspiracy that uses weird tech to allow its hunters to astrally project and gain other quasi-ghostly powers. Geist the Sin-Eaters refers to a Sin-Eater conspiracy in much the same place and time, and I suggested that the former was an attempt to replicate the abilities of the latter.* But if that's so, there's no reason to rule out the Sin-Eaters actually cooperating with such an endeavour (maybe even kicking it off) - in which case, KSI-21 might still have Sin-Eaters in it working alongside the projecting humans.<br /> <br /> * In hindsight, bet they made some Deviants along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they clearly getting their powers from, and still influenced by, Ghosts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:47:31-08:00","id":1181783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1181708#post1181708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because seriously - if any Hunter group that had some involvement with monsters applied, there would be no distinction because they would all be guilty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about &quot;some involvement,&quot; I'm talking about a group with both human and werewolf members. That's well beyond what most groups are. (Cell or compact would be defined by how numerous they are - a great many Union-esque cells and werewolf packs might decide this is a useful alliance to have).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they clearly getting their powers from, and still influenced by, Ghosts? </div> </div> </div>More likely from Sin-Eaters - not as a gift, but via studying and emulating them, but that's still from them - especially if it's study the Sin-Eaters themselves are carrying out in order to recruit more people into their (in Geist terms) krewe than they have geists for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T15:18:00-07:00","id":1203155,"title":"","content":"I think there is one in the Princess the Hopeful, Hunter supplement: The Magisters of the Economy or some such. They knowingly work for Jailers and use an Endowment that lets the Jailers brainwash people into their servants.<br /> <br /> \u200b... Also, while this isn't exactly relevant, I do have this theory that The Talbot Group, especially the Conciliators Methodology, are receiving extra finance support and personal from the Forsaken (probably Iron Masters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 04-04-2018, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T15:43:46-07:00","id":1203163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1178534-cancer-conspiracies?p=1203155#post1203155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is one in the Princess the Hopeful, Hunter supplement: The Magisters of the Economy or some such. They knowingly work for Jailers and use an Endowment that lets the Jailers brainwash people into their servants.<br /> <br /> \u200b... Also, while this isn't exactly relevant, I do have this theory that The Talbot Group, especially the Conciliators Methodology, are receiving extra finance support and personal from the Forsaken (probably Iron Masters).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Magisters would count. The Free Company/Crown Jewels too, if they were a full Conspiracy. The Remnant Pact <i>might</i> depending on how they go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}